s (called [[Harp]], [[Cittern]] and [[Lute]]) [[Span (architecture)|spanning]] the main [[canal]] of the [[Haarlemmermeer]], [[Netherlands]]
* 2005, [[Turning Torso]], [[Malmö]], [[Sweden]]

=== Under construction/Proposed ===
* [[World Trade Center Transportation Hub]], [[New York City]], [[United States|USA]]
* [[Atlanta Symphony Center]], [[Atlanta, Georgia]], [[United States|USA]]
* [[TGV]] Train Station, [[Liège (city)|Liège]], [[Belgium]]
* Palacio de Congresos, [[Oviedo]], Spain
* [[Fordham Spire]], [[Chicago]], [[United States|USA]]
* Margaret Hunt Hill bridge, [[Dallas, Texas|Dallas]], [[Texas]], [[United States|USA]]

Calatrava has also submitted designs for a number of notable projects which were eventually awarded to other designers, including the [[Reichstag (building)|Reichstag]] in Berlin and the [[East London River Crossing]]. The East London River Crossing, in particular, was a very elegant and bold design which was considered by most to be a far more worthy design to the one actually built.

==See also==
[[:Category:Santiago Calatrava structures]]

==Awards==
* 2005 [[American Institute of Architects|AIA]] Gold Medal

==Exhibits==
A special exhibition is being presented at the [[Metropolitan Museum of Art]] through March 5, 2006 [http://www.metmuseum.org/special/Calatrava/architecture_more.asp]. [http://www.metmuseum.org/special/Calatrava/images.asp Images from the exhibition.]

