      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Rollercoaster_dragon_khan_universal_port_aventura_spain.jpg|thumb|The rollercoaster ''Dragon Khan'', the first coaster in the world with eight inversions]]
'''Port Aventura''' is a [[theme park]] in the [[holiday resort]] of [[Salou]], [[Catalonia]], [[Spain]], on the [[Costa Dorada]] (&quot;Gold Coast&quot;). It is 1 hour from Barcelona and has 2 airports within 30 minutes of it. It was conceived and built by the British-based [[Tussauds Group]], but was sold, two years after opening in 1997 to [[Universal]].  It is now owned and operated by a local group of investors, but as of 2004 the Universal name has been dropped from the branding. In 2004 [[NBC Universal]] (Universal Studios' parent) sold all interest in Port Aventura. It was previously called Universal Mediterranea. It is one of the largest in [[Europe]].

Port Aventura is divided into five &quot;worlds&quot; (''Universals''):

* [[American Old West|Far West]]
* [[China]]
* [[Mediterranean]]
* [[Polynesia]]
* [[Mexico]]

Each area is themed according to this scheme and features a variety of rides and attractions. The most notable attractions are:

* [[Dragon Khan]] [[Roller coaster]]
* Tutuki Splash (water-based [[flume]] ride)
* Stampida [[Wooden roller coaster]]
* Hurakan Condor (Tower drop ride)
* [[Templo Del Fuego]] (Indoor special effects show)
* Sea Odyssey (simulator)
* Tomahawk (Small wooden roller coaster)

{{Catalonia-stub}}
{{spain-geo-stub}}

{{Noteworthy Amusement Parks}}

[[Category:Geography of Catalonia]]
[[Category:Amusement parks]]

[[ca:Port Aventura]]
[[de:Universal Mediterrania]]
[[es:Port Aventura]]
[[fr:Port Aventura]]
