  <page>
    <title>Vertical</title>
    <id>229803</id>
    <revision>
      <id>29971169</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-03T01:20:47Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Asahiko</username>
        <id>72441</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>+ja:</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">An object is in a '''vertical''' position when it is aligned in an &quot;up-down&quot; direction, [[perpendicular]] to the [[horizon]].

*In science the vertical (or [[plumb line]]) is the direction of the force of [[gravity]]. 
*A pair of [[angle|angles]] are said to be [[vertical (angles)|vertical]] if they share the same [[vertex]] and are bounded by the same pair of [[Line (mathematics)|lines]] but are opposite to each other.
*In [[music]] the [[vertical (music)|vertical]] aspect is [[simultaneity]], either [[interval (music)|interval]]s or harmony, as opposed to [[succession]] or the [[linear]] aspect
*In [[marketing]] and [[business]] in general, a ''vertical'' informally means a [[vertical market]].

{{disambig}}

[[da:Lodret]]
[[de:Lotrichtung]]
[[eo:Vertikalo]]
[[fr:Vertical]]
[[ja:上下]]
[[nl:Verticaal]]
[[sv:Vertikal]]</text>
    </revision>
