  <page>
    <title>Roy Hudd</title>
    <id>229814</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41764088</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-01T15:59:58Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Bluebot</username>
        <id>527862</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>clean up and bulleting external links using [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser|AWB]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Roy Hudd''' (b. [[May 16]] [[1933]], [[Croydon|Croydon, Surrey]]) is a very tall British radio and television actor. He is also a playwright, author and [[Music Hall]] singer. 

He is best known for his very long-running radio series ''[[The News Huddlines]]'' and recently for his role as the undertaker Archie Shuttleworth in the popular [[ITV]] [[soap opera]] ''[[Coronation Street]]''.

Hudd has written several books on [[Music Hall]] and [[Variety show|Variety]], made Music Hall records and appeared in live [[pantomime]] and variety performances, and is seen by broadcasters as an authority on the subject.

On radio, he has also given his voice to the roles of Max Quordlepleen in ''[[The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy (radio series)|The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy]]'' and James Phillimore in ''The Singular Inheritance of Miss Gloria Wilson,'' an original [[Sherlock Holmes]] radio play. He is due to appear as his hero [[Max Miller]] in a [[Big Finish Productions]] ''[[Doctor Who]]'' [[Doctor Who audio productions|audio play]] ''Pier Pressure'' in [[2006]].

== External links ==
*[http://www.bbc.co.uk/comedy/profiles/roy_hudd.shtml BBC Biography/Profile]

