      <contributor>
        <username>Darwinek</username>
        <id>107928</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>cat</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In the [[Pacific theater]] of [[World War II]], the [[United States|American]] '''Marianas Campaign''', known as ''Operation Forager'', pushed westward from the [[Marshall Islands]] in the summer of [[1944]] to capture the islands of [[Saipan]], [[Tinian]], and [[Guam]].  Another battle of the Marianas campaign was the naval [[Battle of the Philippine Sea]].

==References==
*[http://www.ibiblio.org/hyperwar/PTO/Marianas/index.html Strategic Victory in the Marianas; Liberation of Guam; Capture of Saipan and Tinian]

{{WWII-stub}}

{{commons|Mariana and Palau Islands campaign}}

