'''Nils Jönsson Oxenstierna''', (1390s-1450s) [[Sweden|Swedish]] statesman and co-regent of Sweden, under the [[Kalmar Union]], from January to June of [[1448]], together with his brother [[Bengt Jönsson Oxenstierna]]. Member of the [[Privy Council of Sweden]] at least 1432. Military governor, or ''hövitsman'', at [[Borgholm Castle]] in 1436, [[Stäket]] in 1438, and [[Nyköping Castle]] in 1442. Dubbed as knight by King [[Christopher of Bavaria]] following his coronation in 1441.

