      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Vladikaukaz.jpg|right|thumb|250px|Photo of Vladikavkaz [[mosque]] in [[1912]].]]
'''Vladikavkaz''' ([[Ossetian language|Ossetian]]: Дзæуджыхъæу; {{lang-ru|Владикавка́з}}) is the capital of the [[North Ossetia-Alania|Republic of North Ossetia-Alania]], [[Russia]]. It is situated in the south-east of the republic at the foothills of the [[Caucasus]] mountains, situated on the [[Terek River]], at {{coor dm|43|05|N|44|39|E}}. Its population, which mostly consists of [[Ossetians]], [[Russians]], [[Armenians]] and [[Georgian people|Georgian]]s, is around 312,000 ([[as of 2001]])

The city was founded in [[1784]] as a fortress during the [[Russia]]n conquest of the Caucasus and was for many years the main Russian military base in the region. The [[Georgian Military Highway]], crossing the mountains, was constructed in [[1799]] to link the city with [[Georgia (country)|Georgia]] to the south, and in [[1875]] a railway was built to connect it to [[Rostov-on-Don]] and [[Baku]] in [[Azerbaijan]]. Vladikavkaz has become an important industrial centre for the region, with smelting, refining, chemicals and manufacturing industries.

From [[1931]] to [[1944]] and from [[1954]] to [[1990]] its name was ''Ordzhonikidze'' (Орджоники́дзе) (after [[Grigoriy Ordzhonikidze|Sergo Ordzhonikidze]], a Georgian [[Bolshevik]]), and from [[1944]] to [[1954]] it was called ''Dzaudzhikau'' (Дзауджика́у). Vladikavkaz resumed its old name, which means &quot;Ruler of the Caucasus&quot;, shortly before the fall of the [[Soviet Union]].

Vladikavkaz was fought over in both the [[Russian Civil War]] and [[Second World War]]. In February [[1919]], the anti-Communist [[Volunteer Army]] under General [[Anton Ivanovich Denikin]] seized the city, before being expelled by the [[Red Army]] in March [[1920]]. In November [[1942]], the forces of [[Nazi Germany]] tried unsuccessfully to seize the city but were repelled. This marked the most easterly point ever reached by Nazi forces.

[[Category:North Ossetia]]
[[Category:Cities and towns in Russia]]

