      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Anne Caldwell''' ([[August 30]], [[1867]] - [[October 22]], [[1936]]), also known as '''Anne Caldwell O'Dea''' was a librettist and lyricist. She was born in [[Boston, Massachusetts]]. She wrote both [[pop song]]s and [[Broadway theatre|Broadway]] shows including working with [[Jerome Kern]]. 

