      <text xml:space="preserve">{{Politics of Belgium}}
The '''Humanist Democratic Centre''' ([[French language|French]]: ''Centre Démocrate Humaniste'' or ''CDH'') is a [[centrist]], [[Christian Democracy|Christian Democrat]], [[Belgium|Belgian]] French-speaking [[political party]]. The party held its own in the [[2003]] elections. It is allied to the [[CD&amp;V]] and used to be called the Christian Social Party (French: ''Parti social chrétien'' or ''PSC''). Its ideology is a mix of Christian-inspired [[humanism]], combined with a centrist policy towards the economy, supporting state interventionism and calling for the unity of Belgium.

== Important figures ==
*[[Joëlle Milquet]]

