      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Friedland''' is a [[town]] in the district [[Mecklenburg-Strelitz (district)|Mecklenburg-Strelitz]], [[Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania]], [[Germany]]. It is a local center for some villages like [[Kotelow]], [[Luebbersdorf]], [[Schwichtenberg]], [[Dahle]] and [[Boldekow]], and has approximately 8500 citizens.

It was founded in [[1244]] by the Kurfürsten Otto and Johann of Brandenburg, then having the name ''Vredeland''.

