  <page>
    <title>USS Franklin</title>
    <id>229989</id>
    <revision>
      <id>38982316</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-09T22:53:49Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>N328KF</username>
        <id>77722</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">Five [[United States Navy]] ships have been named '''USS ''Franklin''''', the first four after [[Benjamin Franklin]], and the fifth, the [[aircraft carrier]] CV-13, perpetuating the name of the previous ships (it was not the usual practice at the time to name carriers after individuals).

* The first [[USS Franklin (1775)|''Franklin'']] was a 6-gun [[schooner]], fitted out in 1775 and returned to the owner in [[1776]].

* The second [[USS Franklin (1795)|''Franklin'']] was a 8-gun [[brig]] built in [[1795]], captured by [[Privateer|corsairs]] from [[Tripoli]] in [[1802]], bought back by the Navy in [[1805]], and sold in [[1807]].

* The third [[USS Franklin (1815)|''Franklin'']] was a 74-gun [[ship of the line]] launched in [[1815]] and broken up in [[1852]].

* The fourth [[USS Franklin (1864)|''Franklin'']] was a [[screw frigate]] launched in [[1864]] and in active service until [[1877]], thereafter used as a [[receiving ship]] until [[1915]].

* The fifth [[USS Franklin (CV-13)|''Franklin'' (CV-13)]] was an [[aircraft carrier]] commissioned in [[1944]] and crippled by bombs in March [[1945]], later repaired but remaining in reserve until decommissioning in [[1964]].

* Additionally, a [[ballistic missile submarine]] was named [[USS Benjamin Franklin (SSBN-640)|USS ''Benjamin Franklin'']].

Another ''Franklin'' was the carrier [[USS Franklin D. Roosevelt|''Franklin D. Roosevelt'']].

{{shipindex}}

[[Category:United States Navy ship names|Franklin]]

[[de:USS Franklin]]
[[sl:USS Franklin]]</text>
    </revision>
