      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Elio Di Rupo''' (born [[July 18]], [[1951]]) is the leader of the [[French language|French]]-speaking [[Belgium|Belgian]] [[Socialist Party]], i.e. the [[Socialist Party (francophone Belgium)|Parti Socialiste]] (PS), and one of [[Belgium]]'s most powerful and popular [[politician]]s. 

Elio Di Rupo is a flamboyant left-winger, and is widely considered to have played a major part in the resurgence of the PS, now the joint largest party in the Belgian parliament.

In [[1996]], he was wrongly accused of having had sex with minors by a young gay, Olivier Trusgnach. The allegations nearly put an end to his political career, but a judicial investigation cleared his name. Although Di Rupo is openly gay, no proof was ever found of sexual misconduct with minors.

He is a deputy (MP) for the [[Hainaut]] division of [[Wallonia]]. He once described [[François Mitterrand]] as being &quot;a character from a novel&quot;.

In October [[2005]], he became [[List of Minister-Presidents of Wallonia|Minister-President of Wallonia]] after [[Jean-Claude Van Cauwenberghe]] resigned amid a corruption scandal.

{{start box}}
{{succession box | title=[[List of Minister-Presidents of Wallonia|Minister-President of Wallonia]] | before=[[Robert Collignon]] | after=[[Jean-Claude Van Cauwenberghe]] | years=1999&amp;ndash;2000}}
{{incumbent succession box| title=[[List of Minister-Presidents of Wallonia|Minister-President of Wallonia]] | before=[[Jean-Claude Van Cauwenberghe]] | after=[[Walter Runciman, 1st Viscount Runciman of Doxford|Walter Runciman]] | start=2005}}
{{end box}}

