      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''Diez Estudios Escénicos''''' [Ten scenic Etudes] is a musical work for the stage by [[Juan Maria Solare]].  

It was first performed at Cologne-Mollina, June-July 1996, and is 20'00&quot; in length, without text. For two actors, one actress, diverse objects and instrumental sextet: violin, doublebass, horn, bass clarinet, vibraphone and piano. It is dedicated to [[Mauricio Kagel]].


