|[[Jerry Nelson]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (1976, 2002) A memorable but shortlived character, the 1976 Genie is a different Muppet than the 2002  Genie, who abandoned Aladdin ([[David Alan Grier]]) for a day. Both, however, have the same voice.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Dr. Gina Jefferson'''
|[[Alison Bartlett-O'Reilly]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Proprietor of [[Hooper's Store]], university student,  veternarian. Known generally just as '''Gina''', is a long-time human character on ''Sesame Street''. Debuting as a  teen, Gina has essentially grown up on ''Sesame Street'', just as Maria had before her. Her first appearance was in  1987, when she was hired to assist then-operator of [[Hooper's Store]], [[David (Sesame Street)|David]]. In episode 3179, Elmo actually falls in love with, and wants to marry Gina. Gina has  to kindly explain to him about their age difference.

Gina eventually went to vet school, returning to operate an animal hospital on Sesame Street since 3 January 2001, episode 3918. She is seen briefly in the 35th  anniversary special ''The Street We Live On'', but appearance since are scarce.

The classic ''[[Sesame Street]]'' video title ''[[Best of Ernie and Bert]]'' features Gina in the main plotline, carried on throughout the highlighted skits.

Gina has a niece named Hannah, who with her parents, moved to Sesame Street in January 2001, episode 3923.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Aunt Gisele'''
|[[n/a]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Zoe's aunt from a town called [[Swan Lake]]. See [[Zoe]].

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| [[Image:TV sesame street alan with cow.jpg|125px|Alan and Gladys the cow on Sesame Street.]]
|'''[[Gladys the Cow]]'''
|[[Jennifer Barnhart]] (2003 on)
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (197?-1992, 2003) Overly dramatic bovine. Originally Muppeteered by [[Richard Hunt (puppeteer)|Richard Hunt]] (1971-1992).  Character replaced in 2005 by Cathleen the Cow.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Googel]]'''
|[[?]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (2001-200?) Monster member of ''Monster's Clubhouse''. Contrary to popular belief endorsed by [[The Internet Movie Database|IMDb]],  the character is not named &quot;[[Google]]&quot;, like the popular search engine.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Gordon Robinson]]'''
|[[Roscoe Orman]] (1974 on)
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| One of the longest-lasting characters on ''Sesame Street'', Gordon is a bald African-American teacher,  married to Susan Robinson. He and Susan adopted Miles Robinson as a baby. His birthday is February 24th. Gordon was  portrayed by the late [[Matt Robinson]] from 1969-1971.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Granny Bird'''
|[[?]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Big Bird's grandmother.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Granny Fanny Nesselrode]]'''
|[[Jim Henson]] (1971-198?)
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| An elderly Muppet human. She presumably is an actual grandmother, but of what if any character is  unknown.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| [[Image:Tv sesame street grover and girl.jpg|125px|Grover and a girl on ''[[Sesame Street]]'']]
|'''[[Grover]]'''
|[[Eric Jacobson]] (1997, 2000-)
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Confident, entrepreneurial blue monster. Originally Muppeteered by [[Frank Oz]] (1969-2000).

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| [[Image:Tv sesame street grovers mom.jpg|125px|Grover's mommy.]]
|'''[[Grover's Mommy]]'''
|[[Alice Dinnean Vernon]] (2001 season)
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Grover's mother, generally seen only in books. Her appearance in 2004 video ''[[A Celebration of Me, Grover]]'' was Muppeteered by a separate, unknown actor.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| [[Image:Tv sesame street grundgetta.jpg|125px|Grungetta at her boyfriend's can.]]
|'''[[Grundgetta]]'''
|[[Pam Arciero]] (1984-1999, 2003, 2004, 2005-on)
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| [[Oscar the Grouch]]'s continued girlfriend. Originally Muppeteered by [[Brian Muehl]] (1982-1984).

She was retired from the show in 1999, when [[puppeteer]] Arceiro left to join the cast of ''[[Avenue Q]]''. Grungetta made a background appearance in a 2003 and a 2004 episode. She rejoined the cast in season 36 (2005), as a candidate in &quot;The Grouch Apprentice&quot; skit.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Guy Smiley]]'''
|[[Jim Henson]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (1970-1990) Game show host.

|}

