|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;|[[Image:Fg sesamo grd 16.jpg|125px|Sherlock Hemlock.]]
|'''Sherlock Hemlock'''
|[[Jerry Nelson]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (1970-1992) The character of Sherlock Hemlock spoofs the famous fictional detective [[Sherlock Holmes]]. His assistant, Watson, is a dog who frequently solves the case long before Hemlock, but is unable to communicate this to his master.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Simon the Soundman]]'''
|[[?]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| 

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Slimey'''
|[[?]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Oscar's pet earthworm. His father's name is Dusty, his mother is Eartha, and he has a baby sister, Sloppy, which is short for &quot;Sloppy Jalopy&quot;, Oscar's car on which she was born. A multiepisode plot line on the show, during the mid-[[1990s]], had Slimey traveling to the [[moon]] in a rocket built by &quot;WASA&quot;.

In season 36, Oscar sang the &quot;Worm Workout Song&quot;, while Slimey and his worm friends stretch and wiggle. The song was a parody of the song &quot;[[YMCA (song)|YMCA]]&quot;.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Sloppy'''
|[[?]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Slimey's baby sister.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Smart Tina]]'''
|[[?]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Classmate of [[Roosevelt Franklin]].

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Sonny Friendly'''
|[[Richard Hunt (puppeteer)|Richard Hunt]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (1986-1992, 1996) Game show host. Sonny was created before Jim Henson's death, but after Jim's passing and thus Guy Smiley's retirement, the character of Friendly became all the more used and relevant. However, two years after Jim's death, Richard also passed away. In 1996, [[David Rudman]] took over the character for a few final skits.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''Stinky the Stinkweed'''
|[[Joey Mazzarino]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| (1993 on) A talking, peturbed, smelly plant, that sat on the window of [[123 Sesame Street, New York, New York|123 Sesame Street]] for many years.

|-
|rowspan=&quot;2&quot;| No pic
|'''[[Susan Robinson]]'''
|[[Loretta Long]]
|-
|colspan=&quot;2&quot;| Adoptive mother of Miles Robinson, husband of Gordon Robinson. Susan's birthday is May 4th.

|}

